\f0\fs38 \cf2 \cb3 Reading about twelve infrastructure primitives is useful. Knowing which ones your system is actually missing is what changes what you build next week. This piece comes with an audit prompt and a skill package, and they do different jobs. The audit prompt runs as a structured interview in any model \'97 ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini \'97 where you describe your agent system, answer targeted follow-up questions about how it handles sessions, permissions, crash recovery, and cost tracking, and get back a tiered gap analysis with severity ratings and a prioritized build order. You don\'92t need to prepare anything or share code. If your honest answer to \'93what happens when your agent crashes mid-task?\'94 is \'93the user starts over,\'94 that\'92s a finding, and the audit tells you exactly what to build and in what order. For developers who want the deeper version \'97 something that reads your actual codebase and evaluates against every dimension in this article \'97 the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/NateBJones-Projects/OB1/tree/main/skills/n-agentic-harnesses"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b \cf2 \cb3 \ul \ulc2 \strokec2 skill package}}\'a0covers that for both Claude Code and OpenAI Codex.\
