\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Within hours of the leak going public, tweets cataloguing the unshipped features (background agents running 24/7, coordinator mode, voice commands, browser control via Playwright) were pulling hundreds of thousands of views. \'93It\'92s all built,\'94 one viral thread concluded. \'93They\'92re just drip-feeding releases.\'94 Repos archiving the code hit 30,000 stars within hours.\
And there\'92s a particular irony underneath the frenzy: Anthropic built an entire subsystem called Undercover Mode to prevent their AI from accidentally leaking internal information in public repositories. And then they shipped the entire source code in a\'a0
\f4 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 .map
\f0 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0file. Probably bundled by Claude itself.\
